 (rc msg)←{attachments}SendMail(INI subject body cc);parms;myConnection;mailParms;log;S;convert;this
⍝ Sends a single email via the SMTP server defined in the "EMAIL" section of `INI`.
⍝ This is the common part of `SendMail_CrashReport`, `SendMail_DeletedPkg` and
⍝ `SendMail_PublishedPkg`: those decide whether an email is sent at all and what it says.
⍝ * `subject` is a simple character vector
⍝ * `body` is a simple character vector or a vector of character vectors
⍝ * `cc` may be empty, a character vector or a vector of character vectors. More than one
⍝   address is fine: they are handed over comma-separated, and all of them get the email.
⍝ `attachments`, if specified, must be a vector of (filename mimeType) pairs.
⍝ The idea is to have a GMail address dedicated for http://[test].tatin.dev
⍝ but we use this only to logon the Google's SMTP server: the address is not monitored.
⍝ That way we don't have to be particularly concerned regarding the password.
 attachments←{0<⎕NC ⍵:⍎⍵ ⋄ ⍬}'attachments'
 S←##.##.SMTP
 convert←{0=≢⍵:⍵ ⋄ ⊃{⍺,',',⍵}/⊆⍵}
 parms←⎕NEW S.ConnectionParameters
 parms.Server←⊃INI.Get'EMAIL:SMTP_Server'
 parms.Port←⊃INI.Get'EMAIL:Port'
 parms.Userid←⊃INI.Get'EMAIL:To'
 parms.Password←⊃INI.Get'EMAIL:Password'
 myConnection←⎕NEW S.Connection(,⊂parms)
 mailParms←⎕NEW S.MailParameters
 mailParms.From←'do-not-reply@tatin.dev'
 mailParms.To←⊃INI.Get'EMAIL:To'
 mailParms.CC←convert cc
 mailParms.Subject←subject
 mailParms.Body←body
 :For this :In attachments
     mailParms.AddAttachment this
 :EndFor
 (rc msg log)←myConnection.Send mailParms
 :If 0=rc
     msg←'Email was sent successfully'
 :Else
     msg←'Failed with rc=',(⍕rc),'; ',¯1↓(⊆msg),¨⎕UCS 13
 :EndIf
⍝Done
